  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I verified TX-0401 in account ACC-1005 (EUR):\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Direction:** Outgoing card payment\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also noticed TX-0402, dated 2026-07-14, for the same amount (EUR 240.00) at the same merchant, TechMart Online. It is also settled.\n\nBased on the five dispute reason codes available to me, these could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 match on merchant and amount, so this is worth checking first if you made only one purchase.\n2. **fraud_card_not_present:** A card payment was made without your authorization, for example online, by phone, or by mail order, using your card details.\n3. **unauthorized_debit:** Money left your account without your permission. This is a broader option than the card-fraud code.\n4. **goods_not_received:** You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nTell me which situation matches what happened, and I can check whether a dispute is eligible for that reason code before anything is filed. I will not open a dispute without your confirmation.",
